{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The sanctuary of El, the king of Edom.</b> Kadesh is the name of a city. And it is not Kadesh Barnea, for Kadesh Barnea is a wilderness, as is said (Psalms 29:8): ״יחיל ה׳ מדבר קדש״ — 'the voice of HaShem makes the wilderness of Kadesh shake.' And I have already mentioned this above." "<b>Thus says your brother Israel.</b> That is to say: we were brothers, the children of Abraham, concerning whom it was said (Genesis 15:13): ״כי גר יהיה זרעך״ — 'know that your seed shall be strangers'; and upon both of us was the debt laid to repay. <b>You know all the trouble that has found us.</b> Therefore your father departed from our father, as is said (Genesis 36:6): ״וילך אל ארץ מפני יעקב אחיו״ — 'and he went to another land because of Jacob his brother' — because of the bond of debt laid upon him, and he cast it upon Jacob alone; therefore we have suffered many evils."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:17.198318471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}